 villain and this is of course what  makes akasa's life and his backstory so  compelling and heartbreaking even after  becoming a demon akaza seemed to hold on  to some shred of his humanity because he  absolutely refused to hurt women muzon  even gave akas a special permission to  spare women because of how adamant akaza  was about not hurting them  next up let's talk about a man who  makassa absolutely despises upper moon  to doma doma was born with insanely rare  rainbow colored eyes and pristine white  hair which made people start worshipping  him as some sort of supernatural being  his own parents convinced themselves  that doma could hear the voices of gods  and so they created the paradise faith  religion around him doma never heard the  voices of gods and he found it  ridiculous that fully grown adults would  believe this stuff and that they would  worship him even though he was just a  clueless kid he thought all these people  were crazy because he himself didn't  even believe in paradise he believed it  was all just fairy tales while doma was  still fairly young his mother found out  that his father was cheating on her with  female followers of the cult she flew  into a rage and stabbed him to death  before taking her own life you might  expect doma to be shocked or sad or  traumatized after this happened but he  wasn't his first thought was that his  mother shouldn't have made such a mess  in the room and that someone now has to  clean up all that blood it's clear that  normal human emotions meant nothing to  doma even before he became a demon doma  always had sociopathic tendencies and  this was only exacerbated once he met  muzon and became a demon at the age of  20. after becoming a demon doma became  immortal and since he never believed in  paradise or an afterlife of any kind  dolma developed the sick belief that  because everyone fears death they could  just live forever through him after he  devours them and because his victims are  no longer afraid of anything or  suffering in any way after they are  eaten doma believes that he is actually  saving them by devouring them for  generations doma used his cult to  attract female followers whom he would  then manipulate and devour and not only  would he do this without any empathy or  remorse but he actually felt good about  doing it because he believed that he was  offering salvation to these women some  15 years after the beginning of the  story inosca's own mother fell victim to  doma inosuka's mother was only around 17  or 18 years old when she decided to  escape from her abusive husband who  would beat her up every day she had no  family and no one to turn to so she  sought help and shelter from the  paradise faith for her and her baby she  had been beaten so badly that she had  gone blind in one eye and her entire  face was swollen but once she healed up  doma thought that she was quite  beautiful her name was kotoha and  inosuke actually looks a lot like her  according to doma he wasn't planning on  devouring inosuka's mother because he  liked having her around but kotoha  realized that doma was secretly  devouring his female followers kotoha  couldn't just stand by and watch this  happen so she confronted doma and tried  to flee the temple doma didn't want her  to reveal the truth about him so he  cornered her in the woods and killed her  right before his mother was killed baby  nosuke fell from a cliff and into a body  of water doma just assumed that the baby  had died but instead the baby survived  and was raised in the wilderness by wild  boars after killing kotoha doma devoured  her according to doma koto has life was  miserable and meaningless but because he  devoured her she could now live forever  inside of him not only was doma  unashamed about what he did to kotoha  but he eventually bragged about it to  enosuke during the infinity castle arc  doma is known for targeting women  especially those with strong and healthy  bodies and he enjoys pretending like the  other upper moons are his precious  comrades but that is certainly not the  case and some of the upper moons such as  akaza genuinely hate him doma was also  the one who killed the shinobu's sister  kanae several years before the beginning  of the demonstrator story  finally we have the strongest upper  demon moon a powerful demon slayer  turned demonic traitor upper moon 1  kokushibo kokushibo was born almost 5  centuries ago and his birth name was  michikatsu tsugikuni michikatsu had a  younger twin brother and the twins name  was yorichi togikuni the same yorichi  who would go on to become the strongest  demon player and the original breath of  the sun user michikatsu and yorichi came  from a prominent samurai family and at  this time during the sengoku period  having twins was actually considered a  bad thing since they are born at  practically the same time which could  result in fights over who will inherit  the father's land and titles to make  things worse this was a very  superstitious time and yorichi was born  with a strange birthmark on his face and  so the father decided that the best  thing to do would be to simply eliminate  lilo yorichi and keep michikatsu  thankfully michikawrichi's mother  refused to let this happen and she  became so angry and aggressive that her  husband agreed to spare yorichi's life  instead of eliminating the younger twin  the family would raise him until he  reached the age of 10 and then they  would send him away to a temple where he  would become a monk due to the fact that  monks usually have to renounce all of  their worldly possessions yorichi would  no longer have any claim to the family's  land and titles and so michikatsu would  be able to succeed his father as the  head of the family without any problems  and so the two twins were raised  completely differently michikatsu was  groomed to be the head of the family and  he had better living quarters better  clothes better food better education and  so on and while michikatsu was busy  preparing himself to one day succeed his  father yurichi became extremely attached  to their mother and he would always  cling to her left side michikatsu felt  bad for his little brother so he would  often sneak into his brother's room in  order to play with him michikatsu wasn't  able to give yorichi any of his  possessions because their father would  notice and get angry so michikatsu gave  his brother a small wooden flute that he  had made himself now yurichi wasn't  exactly a normal child and this further  contributed to his black sheep status  for instance he never smiled not even as  a baby and he didn't even speak until  the age of seven everyone basically  concluded that yorichi must be deaf and  so he would never be able to speak  properly but as it turns out yorichi  wasn't deaf as his brother learned one  day when he was practicing with his  sword in the garden yurichi was just  standing silently behind michikatsu and  watching him but then suddenly he  actually said something he said my  brother is your dream to become the  strongest samurai in the nation  michikatsu was so surprised to hear his  brother actually speaking that he gasped  and dropped his wooden sword yorichi  then said that he also wanted to become  a samurai but michikatsu knew that when  he turned 10 yorichi would be sent to a  temple he was destined to become a monk  not a samurai then michikatsu saw his  brother smile for the very first time  and to him this was an odd and  unsettling sight after this yorichi  started hanging around his brother and  the family's swordsmanship instructor  during their swordsmanship training and  he expressed a desire to learn the way  of the sword the instructor didn't see  any harm in letting yurichi practice  with them so he gave him a wooden  practice sword but after only a few  words of basic instruction the  instructor asked yurichi to try and hit  him michikatsu wasn't expecting anything  much because he himself had never  succeeded in landing a single hit on  their instructor no matter how hard he  tried but then the seven-year-old  yoricci managed to land four strong  blows on their instructor in the blink  of an eye and these four strikes were so  strong that they knocked the instructor  out yurichi's blows didn't break any  bones or cause any permanent damage but  they left massive lumps on the  instructor's body in the places where  the wood had hit following this incident  yorichi stopped saying that he wanted to  become a samurai he hated the feeling of  hitting someone and he didn't want  anything to do with that type of life  but michikatsu was amazed and he wanted  to know the secret behind yurichi's  strength so he kept pushing him to  explain how he became so strong  that is when we learned that even as a  kid yorichi could see into the  transparent world so he could anticipate  his opponent's movements based on the  position of their bones the contractions  of their muscles the flow of their blood  and so on yorichi was also born with  exceptional strength and speed and that  is when michikatsu came to a startling  conclusion all this time he had felt  sorry for his younger brother but the  truth was that yorici was actually much  more talented than he was now michikatsu  worked hard and he had talent so he  certainly made progress and he became  stronger unfortunately for him his  progress was nothing compared to yurichi  who was just an unrivaled genius and  even though yorichi wasn't interested in  the samurai life anymore after the  instructor told their father about  yorichi's unsurpassed talent the father  abruptly changed his mind about his  successor he now wanted the incredibly  strong and talented yorichi to take over  as the head of the family instead of  michikatsu and michikatsu was now forced  to sleep in that small isolated room  where yorichi had been sleeping all this  time to make things even worse  michikatsu was now going to be sent to a  temple when he turned 10 instead of  yorichi which meant that michikatsu's  lifelong dream of becoming a samurai was  now impossible but then one night  yorichi came to tell michikatsu that  their mother had died michikatsu was  shaken by this revelation because he  didn't think that there was anything  wrong with their mother but yorichi just  told them to ask her servant about the  details because he will now be departing  for the temple michikatsu was confused  since yorichi was no longer being forced  to be a monk but yorichi knew that his  father was now planning to send  michikatsu instead of him and so he  decided to go before their father could  do that yorichi said that he will bring  that wooden flute that michikatsu had  made for him so that he could feel like  his older brother was always with him  and then he left michikatsu thought that  flute was poorly made and a piece of  junk and he was surprised to see orichi  acting like it was some sort of treasure  after yorici left michikatsu read his  mother's journal and that's when he  realized that his mother had been  suffering from an illness for years and  that yorichi had sensed it this illness  was affecting the left side of their  mother's body so when yorici was  clinging to that side he wasn't really  clinging he was actually helping to  support her because her body had been  weakened by illness  that is the point at which michikatsu  fully understood that yarichi was far  more observant and talented and  compassionate than him yorichi just  seemed to be good at everything and  because of this michikatsu began to burn  with jealousy he even began to feel  hatred for his own brother because he  just couldn't accept that no matter how  hard he tried yorichi would always be  better than him at everything this is  ironic because back when yorici was  being treated as the black sheep of the  family michikatsu felt sorry for him and  he tried to help him but it seems that  in his own mind michikatsu had also  accepted the idea that he was superior  to yorichi so when the tables turned  then yorichi showed himself to be  superior and then everyone started  treating him as superior michikatsu's  ego couldn't handle it and he began  wishing that his brother had never been  born luckily michikatsu's jealousy  subsided after yurichi disappeared from  his life yorichi had vanished and no one  could locate him so michikatsu's father  had no choice but to make michikatsu his  heir once again ten years passed then  michikatsu settled down and started a  family his days were quiet and boring  and he enjoyed a comfortable and  uneventful life however that comfort was  broken when a demon attacked michikatsu  and his men in the forest the demon  killed michikatsu's men and he was about  to kill him too when an adult yorichi  showed up and took the demon down in an  instant  the moment that michikatsu saw his  brother again he knew that yurichi had  mastered the sword and that he was an  incredible warrior michikatsu's serenity  was destroyed once again and he began to  burn with jealousy yorichi was  unbelievably strong and he had an  impeccable character and michikatsu  decided that he would do anything to  become as strong and as skilled as his  brother michikatsu went so far as to  abandon his family and dedicate his  whole life to following in yorichi's  footsteps and becoming a demon slayer  michikatsu trained under yurichi and he  learned breathing techniques directly  from his brother but none of the other  demon slayers michikatsu included were  able to attain the full extent of  yorichi's power they could never  reproduce the breathing technique that  he used the breath of the sun so yorichi  changed the breathing techniques  slightly as he taught them in order to  make it possible for them to actually  learn and master these techniques that  is how all the many derivatives of sun  breathing emerged and one of those  derivatives was michikatsu's own moon  breathing eventually michikatsu  manifested a demon's layer mark  identical to the one that his brother  was born with and i mean when you take  everything into consideration michikatsu  was an incredibly powerful swordsman and  demonstrator but despite his impressive  strength which was far far above average  mijikatsu still couldn't come even close  to matching yorichi no matter how hard  he trained and no matter how much of his  life he dedicated to getting stronger  michikatsu was simply unable to learn  sun breathing and he could never rival  the superhuman abilities of his brother  and then there was another major problem  all the demon slayers who had managed to  manifest the demon's hair mark began to  die off after reaching the age of 25.  the demon sailor mark allowed the slayer  to unlock more power but in exchange for  that power it drastically reduced the  demon slayer's lifespan michika to  realize that he was going to die without  ever even coming close to achieving his  dream of becoming the strongest samurai  and surpassing his brother and in that  moment of weakness and desperation he  was approached by the crafty demon king  muza muzan told michikatsu that if he  became a demon he could live forever and  he wouldn't have to worry about dying at  the age of 25 he would also have a much  stronger body and he would have all of  eternity to become stronger than yurichi  and so even though he dedicated his  whole life to ridding the world of  demons michikatsu's jealousy got the  best of him he agreed to consume muzan's  blood and become a demon in exchange for  eternal life and super human power that  is when michikatsu tsugikuni became  kokushibo and yet even after 60 years of  being a demon kokushibo still couldn't  overcome yorichi the two brothers faced  off against each other when yorichi was  already in his mid-80s unlike the other  demon slayers who manifested the  demonstra mark yorichi did not die at  the age of 25. this tells us yet again  that yorichi was simply not the average  demon player he was always special since  he was a demon kokushibo didn't age and  he was still at peak strength even  though he should have been like 85 years  old meanwhile yorichi who was not a  demon really was 85 years old and he was  now a frail old man and yet even after  six decades yorichi was still stronger  than kokushibo his technique was so  exceptional that he defeated the demon  kokushibo despite his advanced age  kokushibo was down for the count and at  yorichi's mercy but then yorichi died of  old age before he could strike the  finishing blow against his brother and  so kokushiba lost the battle but he  managed to survive this meant that for  the next 400 years kukushibo had to live  with the knowledge that even as an old  man yurichi was still far stronger than  him  and if all of this wasn't bad enough  when kokushibo cut down yorichi's  lifeless body following yurichi's death  he found that small wooden flute that he  had made for his brother back when they  were children yorichi still treasured  that stupid crappy flute that his twin  brother had made for him all those years  ago and that's despite the fact that  this same brother betrayed the demon  slayers and became a ruthless demon so  not only was yurichi still stronger than  kokushibo even though he was a human in  his 80s and kokushiba was an immortal  demon  but yorichi was also a man of impeccable  character and boundless compassion  something that kokushibo could never  hope to be kokushi was jealousy  destroyed his honor his character and  his compassion and so no matter how many  centuries kokushiba would ultimately get  to live his long-dead brother would  always remain superior to him not only  in strength but in all those categories  as well  and that is it  every upper moon's backstory in demon  slayer explained which was your favorite  backstory out of all the upper moons let  me know down below if you're looking for  a video to watch next i also have a 